 a beta of 0.91, it moves roughly with the market.","About $33.8M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 49% in the 2020 crash and 38% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The stock trades 44% below its DCF fair value of $137, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 20%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $95.44 to $199 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Industrials peers: EV/EBITDA 10.2 vs 13.3 and P/FCF 14.0 vs 22.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 41% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 7.1% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 6.0% (vs the 8% bar).","The 11 covering analysts target $89.55 on average, 18% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 7% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.2%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.41).","It converts 4% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 8/9 and cash conversion of 2.34x.","ROE of 7% is amplified by 3.0x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 0.3% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 5.2x net debt to EBITDA ($261.1M of cash against $1.1B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 2.5x.","Its debt comes due soon (maturity wall about 1.4 years out), so refinancing terms matter.","Goodwill makes up 51% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 15.7% over 3 years, 26.3% over 5 years and 14.3% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 20%).","At current returns, reinvesting 74% of profits supports about 4.9% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 23.3% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 0.98, a backlog worth 75% of annual revenue and deferred revenue down 22%.","Capex runs only 0.7x depreciation (0.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 30, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (1.0%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.3% (1.3% in buybacks).","The share count has grown 21.7% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","Short interest is elevated at 11.4% of the float, 3.9 days to cover."],"people":["With about 16,200 employees, each generates about $277K of revenue, 0.8x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 12.7% a year.","That works out to $10K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.0M (11x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":60,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but it earns less than its cost of capital.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 51, gates 11/24)","Trades 44% below fair value of $137","Revenue grew 26.3%/yr over 5y","Piotroski F-score 8/9","EV/EBITDA 10.2x vs sector 13.3x"],"cons":["ROIC 6.7% vs WACC 8.2%","Net debt/EBITDA 5.2x","Interest coverage only 2.5x","Heavy insider selling ($174.3M net over 12 months)"],"flags":[],"need":["it earns less than its cost of capital"],"buy_below":116.24,"vc":{"base":136.76,"base_src":"dcf","bear":95.44,"bull":198.76,"alt_median":26.07,"n_alt":2,"gap":4.246,"dispersion":0.1972,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 425% above the other models' median ($26.07)"]},"med":{"pe":23.2692,"ev_ebitda":13.319,"pfcf":22.2778,"pb":3.0551,"roic":0.1001,"gross_margin":0.2851,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0147}},"ticker":"VVX","date":"2026-11-06"}